[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62598,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperreactio luteinalis is bilateral ovarian enlargement due to numerous luteinized follicle cysts related to pregnancy. Ovulation induction may result in a similar condition (ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome).</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62599,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62600,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>GA18.1 Corpus luteum cyst</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62601,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> theca lutein cysts; multiple luteinized follicle cysts; ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62602,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62603,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ovary</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62604,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperreactio luteinalis occurs during the second or third trimester of pregnancy; it may be asymptomatic or may cause abdominal pain due to ovarian torsion or rupture {26474228}. Rare cases may be associated with maternal or fetal virilization, pre-eclampsia, thyroid abnormalities, or gestational diabetes {23804351; 22338557}. Ultrasound shows bilateral enlarged ovaries with multiple cysts without a solid component (spoke-wheel appearance) {23804351}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62605,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperreactio luteinalis is rare. Ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome is more frequent in patients undergoing treatment for infertility.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62606,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperreactio luteinalis is usually associated with an abnormally elevated hCG level due to gestational trophoblastic disease, fetal hydrops, or multiple gestations, but it may also develop during a spontaneously conceived singleton pregnancy {26474228; 30167380}. Ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome may occur after ovulation induction with FSH, hCG or clomifene.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62607,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Rare patients with familial spontaneous ovarian hyperstimulation syndrome have a mutation in the FSH receptor leading to hypersensitivity to hCG {12930927}. The exact mechanism by which the increased hCG levels (or hypersensitivity to hCG) result in ovarian hyperstimulation is unknown.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62608,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hyperreactio luteinalis manifests as enlargement of ovaries, with multiple thin-walled cysts filled with clear or haemorrhagic fluid.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62609,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histopathology reveals ovaries with multiple cystic follicles lined by luteinized granulosa and theca interna cells in an oedematous stroma. Aggregates of luteinized stromal cells are often seen between cysts.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62610,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62611,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62612,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> classic clinical and ultrasonographic presentation.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> excision and histological examination is rarely necessary&nbsp;&ndash; if excised, the specimen shows multiple cystic follicles lined by luteinized granulosa and theca interna cells in an oedematous ovarian stroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62613,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62614,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 119,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with hyperreactio luteinalis are at risk for pre-eclampsia and preterm delivery. The condition is usually self-limited and can be managed conservatively {21497342}. Surgical intervention is usually limited to cases with torsion or haemoperitoneum.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-14T11:37:54"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]